{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c001",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Empirical Example for Sensitivity Analysis: Gasoline Demand\n",
    "\n",
    "This is an adaptation of the replication package for Chernozhukov, Cinelli, Newey, Sharma and Syrgkanis,\n",
    "*Long Story Short: Omitted Variable Bias in Causal Machine Learning*\n",
    "\n",
    "The original replication package can be found __[here](https://dataverse.harvard.edu/dataset.xhtml?persistentId=doi:10.7910/DVN/VH6QHQ)__.\n",
    "\n",
    "Note: This R notebook implements the sieve Riesz representer approach for the nonparametric estimator. The generalized random forest Riesz representer (ForestRiesz) used in the Python notebook has no direct R equivalent and is omitted here; the sieve candidates (degree-1 and degree-2 polynomial sieves) are used instead."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "c002",
   "metadata": {
    "vscode": {
     "languageId": "r"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "repos <- c(CRAN = \"https://cloud.r-project.org\")\n",
    "pkgs  <- c(\"ranger\", \"glmnet\", \"ggplot2\", \"Matrix\")\n",
    "for (p in pkgs) {\n",
    "  if (!requireNamespace(p, quietly = TRUE))\n",
    "    install.packages(p, repos = repos, quiet = TRUE)\n",
    "}"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "c003",
   "metadata": {
    "vscode": {
     "languageId": "r"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "suppressMessages({\n",
    "  library(ranger)\n",
    "  library(glmnet)\n",
    "  library(ggplot2)\n",
    "})\n",
    "options(scipen = 99)\n",
    "options(repr.plot.width = 5, repr.plot.height = 5, repr.plot.res = 150)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c004",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Setting\n",
    "\n",
    "The data come from the 2001 National Household Travel Survey and contain household gasoline consumption, gasoline prices, income brackets, and 24 observed controls describing population density, urbanization, demographics, and Census regions. After the sample restrictions used in the earlier demand studies, the analysis contains 3,466 households.\n",
    "\n",
    "The outcome $Y$ is log gasoline consumption, the treatment $D$ is log gasoline price, and $X^o$ collects the observed controls. The target is the average causal derivative $\\theta_s = \\mathrm{E}\\{\\partial_d g_s(D, X^o)\\}$, the average price elasticity of gasoline demand. The moment function below encodes $m(W_s, g) = \\partial_d g(D, X^o)$, approximated by a central finite difference with $\\epsilon = 0.01$."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "c005",
   "metadata": {
    "vscode": {
     "languageId": "r"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "moment_fn <- function(X, test_fn, epsilon = 0.01) {\n",
    "  t1 <- cbind(X[, 1L] + epsilon, X[, -1L, drop = FALSE])\n",
    "  t0 <- cbind(X[, 1L] - epsilon, X[, -1L, drop = FALSE])\n",
    "  (test_fn(t1) - test_fn(t0)) / (2 * epsilon)\n",
    "}"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c006",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Data\n",
    "\n",
    "Following the earlier demand studies, households with very low prices or incomes are dropped. Besides the full sample (`q=5`), the analysis uses four income groups. The first three (`q=1,2,3`) are overlapping groups centered near annual incomes of \\$42,500, \\$57,500 and \\$72,500. The fourth (`q=4`) contains high-income households with income above roughly \\$110,000 ($\\log y \\geq 11.6$)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "c007",
   "metadata": {
    "vscode": {
     "languageId": "r"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "get_data_r <- function(q = 5L, synthetic = FALSE, region = TRUE,\n",
    "                        random_seed = 123L) {\n",
    "  data_url <- paste0(\n",
    "    \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/CausalAIBook/MetricsMLNotebooks/\",\n",
    "    \"update-notebooks/data/data_BHP2_with_region.csv\"\n",
    "  )\n",
    "  df <- read.csv(data_url, stringsAsFactors = FALSE)\n",
    "\n",
    "  df <- df[df$log_p > log(1.2), ]\n",
    "  df <- df[df$log_y > log(15000), ]\n",
    "  if (!(q %in% c(4L, 5L))) {\n",
    "    df <- df[df$log_y >= log(42500) - 0.5 & df$log_y <= log(72500) + 0.5, ]\n",
    "  }\n",
    "  if (q == 1L) df <- df[df$log_y >= log(42500)-.5 & df$log_y <= log(42500)+.5, ]\n",
    "  if (q == 2L) df <- df[df$log_y >= log(57500)-.5 & df$log_y <= log(57500)+.5, ]\n",
    "  if (q == 3L) df <- df[df$log_y >= log(72500)-.5 & df$log_y <= log(72500)+.5, ]\n",
    "  if (q == 4L) df <- df[df$log_y >= 11.6, ]\n",
    "\n",
    "  # Drop non-feature columns\n",
    "  drop_cols <- c(\"log_q\", \"distance_oil1000\", \"share\")\n",
    "  Xdf <- df[, !names(df) %in% drop_cols, drop = FALSE]\n",
    "\n",
    "  if (region) {\n",
    "    lvls <- sort(unique(df$region))[-1L]          # drop-first encoding\n",
    "    for (lv in lvls) {\n",
    "      Xdf[[paste0(\"region_\", lv)]] <- as.numeric(df$region == lv)\n",
    "    }\n",
    "  }\n",
    "  Xdf <- Xdf[, !names(Xdf) %in% c(\"state_fips\", \"region\"), drop = FALSE]\n",
    "\n",
    "  X <- as.matrix(Xdf)\n",
    "  y <- df$log_q\n",
    "\n",
    "  # 5-fold state-grouped splits\n",
    "  set.seed(random_seed)\n",
    "  states     <- df$state_fips\n",
    "  state_ids  <- sample(unique(states))\n",
    "  k          <- 5L\n",
    "  fold_label <- rep_len(seq_len(k), length(state_ids))\n",
    "  state_fold <- setNames(fold_label, state_ids)\n",
    "  obs_fold   <- state_fold[as.character(states)]\n",
    "  splits <- lapply(seq_len(k), function(i) {\n",
    "    list(train = which(obs_fold != i), test = which(obs_fold == i))\n",
    "  })\n",
    "\n",
    "  list(X = X, y = y, splits = splits, col_names = colnames(Xdf))\n",
    "}"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "id": "c008",
   "metadata": {
    "vscode": {
     "languageId": "r"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Global parameters\n",
    "q_grid    <- 1:5\n",
    "synthetic <- FALSE\n",
    "region    <- TRUE\n",
    "verbose   <- 0L"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c009",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Module Definitions\n",
    "\n",
    "The following cells implement helper functions used by this notebook. The nonparametric estimator uses polynomial sieve Riesz representers (degree-1 and degree-2) fitted by L2 or elastic-net penalized regression. The partially linear estimator uses random forests for first-stage nuisance estimation."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "id": "c010",
   "metadata": {
    "vscode": {
     "languageId": "r"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Polynomial-treatment x covariate feature matrix (cross product)\n",
    "# Mirrors Python's Featurizer._transform: cross_product(poly(T), X[:,1:])\n",
    "poly_cross_feats <- function(X, degree) {\n",
    "  n   <- nrow(X)\n",
    "  p_x <- ncol(X) - 1L\n",
    "  T_poly <- outer(X[, 1L], seq(0L, degree), `^`)    # n x (degree+1)\n",
    "  feats  <- matrix(0, n, (degree + 1L) * p_x)\n",
    "  for (j in seq_len(degree + 1L)) {\n",
    "    idx <- ((j - 1L) * p_x + 1L):(j * p_x)\n",
    "    feats[, idx] <- T_poly[, j] * X[, -1L, drop = FALSE]\n",
    "  }\n",
    "  cbind(1.0, feats)   # include intercept column\n",
    "}"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "id": "c011",
   "metadata": {
    "vscode": {
     "languageId": "r"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Linear sieve Riesz representer with L2 penalty.\n",
    "# Returns a prediction function function(X_new) -> numeric(nrow(X_new))\n",
    "fit_sieve_rr <- function(X_train, moment_fn, alpha = 0, degree = 1L) {\n",
    "  Xf <- poly_cross_feats(X_train, degree)\n",
    "  n  <- nrow(Xf)\n",
    "  p  <- ncol(Xf)\n",
    "\n",
    "  # Moment features: M[i,j] = moment_fn(X, phi_j) where phi_j(x) = Xf[i,j]\n",
    "  Mf <- matrix(0, n, p)\n",
    "  for (j in seq_len(p)) {\n",
    "    local({\n",
    "      jj <- j\n",
    "      Mf[, jj] <<- moment_fn(X_train,\n",
    "        function(Xnew) poly_cross_feats(Xnew, degree)[, jj])\n",
    "    })\n",
    "  }\n",
    "\n",
    "  Sig    <- crossprod(Xf) / n\n",
    "  reg    <- alpha * diag(p); reg[1L, 1L] <- 0\n",
    "  params <- solve(Sig + reg + 1e-10 * diag(p), colMeans(Mf))\n",
    "\n",
    "  function(Xnew) drop(poly_cross_feats(Xnew, degree) %*% params)\n",
    "}"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "id": "c012",
   "metadata": {
    "vscode": {
     "languageId": "r"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Elastic-net sieve Riesz representer via L-BFGS-B on the doubled variable.\n",
    "# Mirrors Python's SparseSieveRR using scipy fmin_l_bfgs_b.\n",
    "fit_sparse_sieve_rr <- function(X_train, moment_fn,\n",
    "                                 alpha = 0.01, l1_ratio = 1.0,\n",
    "                                 degree = 1L, tol = 1e-4) {\n",
    "  Xf <- poly_cross_feats(X_train, degree)\n",
    "  n  <- nrow(Xf); p <- ncol(Xf)\n",
    "\n",
    "  Mf <- matrix(0, n, p)\n",
    "  for (j in seq_len(p)) {\n",
    "    local({\n",
    "      jj <- j\n",
    "      Mf[, jj] <<- moment_fn(X_train,\n",
    "        function(Xnew) poly_cross_feats(Xnew, degree)[, jj])\n",
    "    })\n",
    "  }\n",
    "\n",
    "  Sig    <- crossprod(Xf) / n\n",
    "  mfeats <- colMeans(Mf)\n",
    "  a_l1   <- alpha * l1_ratio\n",
    "  a_l2   <- alpha * (1 - l1_ratio)\n",
    "\n",
    "  loss_gr <- function(ec) {\n",
    "    coef <- ec[1:p] - ec[(p + 1):(2 * p)]\n",
    "    loss <- -2 * sum(mfeats * coef) + as.numeric(t(coef) %*% Sig %*% coef)\n",
    "    loss <- loss + a_l1 * sum(ec[2:p]) + a_l1 * sum(ec[(p + 2):(2 * p)])\n",
    "    loss <- loss + 0.5*a_l2*sum(ec[2:p]^2) + 0.5*a_l2*sum(ec[(p+2):(2*p)]^2)\n",
    "    gr   <- 2 * as.numeric(Sig %*% coef - mfeats)\n",
    "    grad <- c(gr, -gr)\n",
    "    grad[2:p]             <- grad[2:p]             + a_l1 + a_l2 * ec[2:p]\n",
    "    grad[(p+2):(2*p)] <- grad[(p+2):(2*p)] + a_l1 + a_l2 * ec[(p+2):(2*p)]\n",
    "    list(value = loss, gradient = grad)\n",
    "  }\n",
    "\n",
    "  res <- optim(\n",
    "    rep(0, 2 * p),\n",
    "    fn = function(ec) loss_gr(ec)$value,\n",
    "    gr = function(ec) loss_gr(ec)$gradient,\n",
    "    method  = \"L-BFGS-B\",\n",
    "    lower   = rep(0, 2 * p),\n",
    "    control = list(factr = tol / .Machine$double.eps, maxit = 1000L)\n",
    "  )\n",
    "  params <- res$par[1:p] - res$par[(p + 1):(2 * p)]\n",
    "  function(Xnew) drop(poly_cross_feats(Xnew, degree) %*% params)\n",
    "}"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 9,
   "id": "c013",
   "metadata": {
    "vscode": {
     "languageId": "r"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Riesz score on held-out data: E[2*m(X;g) - g(X)^2]  (higher is better)\n",
    "riesz_score_r <- function(rr_fn, X_val, moment_fn)\n",
    "  mean(2 * moment_fn(X_val, rr_fn) - rr_fn(X_val)^2)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Select best Riesz candidate via CV, return a factory function(X_train) -> rr_fn\n",
    "rr_fn_gen <- function(X, moment_fn, splits, ...) {\n",
    "  alpha_grid <- 10^seq(-5, 2, length.out = 8L)\n",
    "  best_score <- -Inf\n",
    "  best_factory <- NULL\n",
    "\n",
    "  for (degree in c(1L, 2L)) {\n",
    "    for (alpha in alpha_grid) {\n",
    "      for (sparse in c(FALSE, TRUE)) {\n",
    "        scores <- vapply(splits, function(s) {\n",
    "          fit_fn <- if (sparse) fit_sparse_sieve_rr else fit_sieve_rr\n",
    "          m <- tryCatch(\n",
    "            fit_fn(X[s$train, , drop=FALSE], moment_fn,\n",
    "                   alpha=alpha, degree=degree),\n",
    "            error = function(e) NULL)\n",
    "          if (is.null(m)) return(-Inf)\n",
    "          riesz_score_r(m, X[s$test, , drop=FALSE], moment_fn)\n",
    "        }, numeric(1L))\n",
    "        sc <- mean(scores[is.finite(scores)])\n",
    "        if (is.finite(sc) && sc > best_score) {\n",
    "          best_score <- sc\n",
    "          best_factory <- local({\n",
    "            d <- degree; a <- alpha; sp <- sparse\n",
    "            function(X_tr) {\n",
    "              if (sp) fit_sparse_sieve_rr(X_tr, moment_fn, alpha=a, degree=d)\n",
    "              else    fit_sieve_rr(X_tr, moment_fn, alpha=a, degree=d)\n",
    "            }\n",
    "          })\n",
    "        }\n",
    "      }\n",
    "    }\n",
    "  }\n",
    "  if (is.null(best_factory))\n",
    "    best_factory <- function(X_tr)\n",
    "      fit_sieve_rr(X_tr, moment_fn, alpha=1e-2, degree=1L)\n",
    "  best_factory\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "# Regression model selection: ranger vs. lasso (glmnet), return factory\n",
    "reg_fn_gen <- function(X, y, splits, ...) {\n",
    "  # Scale matrix, clamping zero-SD columns to 1 to avoid NaN\n",
    "  safe_scale <- function(X, ctr = colMeans(X),\n",
    "                          scl = { s <- apply(X, 2, sd); s[s < .Machine$double.eps] <- 1; s }) {\n",
    "    scale(X, center = ctr, scale = scl)\n",
    "  }\n",
    "\n",
    "  # Evaluate ranger CV MSE\n",
    "  rf_preds <- numeric(nrow(X))\n",
    "  for (s in splits) {\n",
    "    df_tr <- as.data.frame(cbind(y_tr=y[s$train], X[s$train,,drop=FALSE]))\n",
    "    rf <- ranger(y_tr~., data=df_tr, num.trees=200L, verbose=FALSE)\n",
    "    rf_preds[s$test] <- predict(rf, data=as.data.frame(X[s$test,,drop=FALSE]))$predictions\n",
    "  }\n",
    "  rf_mse <- mean((y - rf_preds)^2)\n",
    "\n",
    "  # Evaluate lasso CV MSE; fall back to ranger if glmnet errors\n",
    "  lasso_fit <- tryCatch(cv.glmnet(safe_scale(X), y, alpha=1, nfolds=5L),\n",
    "                         error = function(e) NULL)\n",
    "  lasso_mse <- if (!is.null(lasso_fit)) min(lasso_fit$cvm) else Inf\n",
    "\n",
    "  if (lasso_mse < rf_mse) {\n",
    "    function(X_tr, y_tr) {\n",
    "      ctr <- colMeans(X_tr)\n",
    "      scl <- apply(X_tr, 2, sd); scl[scl < .Machine$double.eps] <- 1\n",
    "      lf  <- cv.glmnet(scale(X_tr, center=ctr, scale=scl), y_tr, alpha=1, nfolds=5L)\n",
    "      function(Xnew) as.numeric(predict(lf, newx=scale(Xnew, center=ctr, scale=scl), s=\"lambda.min\"))\n",
    "    }\n",
    "  } else {\n",
    "    function(X_tr, y_tr) {\n",
    "      df_tr <- as.data.frame(cbind(y_tr=y_tr, X_tr))\n",
    "      rf <- ranger(y_tr~., data=df_tr, num.trees=200L, verbose=FALSE)\n",
    "      function(Xnew) predict(rf, data=as.data.frame(Xnew))$predictions\n",
    "    }\n",
    "  }\n",
    "}"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
   "id": "c014",
   "metadata": {
    "vscode": {
     "languageId": "r"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Doubly-robust cross-fitted moment estimator.\n",
    "# rr_factory: function(X_train) -> rr prediction function\n",
    "# get_reg_fn: function(X_train, y_train) -> reg prediction function  (pre-built by reg_fn_gen)\n",
    "debiased_moment_fit <- function(X, y, moment_fn, rr_factory, get_reg_fn, splits) {\n",
    "  n   <- nrow(X)\n",
    "  rr_pred <- reg_pred <- moment_pred <- moment_rr <- numeric(n)\n",
    "  reg_fitter <- get_reg_fn   # already the fitter: function(X_tr, y_tr) -> pred_fn\n",
    "\n",
    "  for (s in splits) {\n",
    "    tr <- s$train; te <- s$test\n",
    "    rr_fn  <- rr_factory(X[tr, , drop=FALSE])\n",
    "    reg_fn <- reg_fitter(X[tr, , drop=FALSE], y[tr])\n",
    "\n",
    "    rr_pred[te]     <- rr_fn(X[te, , drop=FALSE])\n",
    "    reg_pred[te]    <- reg_fn(X[te, , drop=FALSE])\n",
    "    moment_pred[te] <- moment_fn(X[te, , drop=FALSE], reg_fn)\n",
    "    moment_rr[te]   <- moment_fn(X[te, , drop=FALSE], rr_fn)\n",
    "  }\n",
    "  moment <- moment_pred + rr_pred * (y - reg_pred)\n",
    "  list(moment=moment, reg_pred=reg_pred, reisz_pred=rr_pred,\n",
    "       moment_reisz=moment_rr, y=y)\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "avg_moment_r <- function(est, alpha = 0.1) {\n",
    "  m  <- mean(est$moment); n <- length(est$moment)\n",
    "  se <- sd(est$moment) / sqrt(n)\n",
    "  h  <- se * qt(1 - alpha/2, n - 1L)\n",
    "  c(point=m, se=se, lower=m-h, upper=m+h)\n",
    "}"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 11,
   "id": "c015",
   "metadata": {
    "vscode": {
     "languageId": "r"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# -- Nonparametric (DebiasedMoment) sensitivity ------------------------------------\n",
    "\n",
    "sensitivity_bounds_single_r <- function(est, eta_ysq, eta_asq, alpha = NULL) {\n",
    "  nusq    <- mean(2*est$moment_reisz - est$reisz_pred^2)\n",
    "  sigmasq <- mean((est$y - est$reg_pred)^2)\n",
    "  S       <- sqrt(sigmasq * nusq)\n",
    "  Casq    <- eta_asq / (1 - eta_asq)\n",
    "  theta   <- mean(est$moment)\n",
    "  error   <- S * sqrt(Casq * eta_ysq)\n",
    "  if (is.null(alpha)) return(c(theta - error, theta + error))\n",
    "  psi_theta   <- est$moment - theta\n",
    "  psi_sigmasq <- (est$y - est$reg_pred)^2 - sigmasq\n",
    "  psi_nusq    <- 2*est$moment_reisz - est$reisz_pred^2 - nusq\n",
    "  k <- sqrt(Casq * eta_ysq) / (2 * S)\n",
    "  phi_p <- psi_theta + k * (sigmasq*psi_nusq + nusq*psi_sigmasq)\n",
    "  phi_m <- psi_theta - k * (sigmasq*psi_nusq + nusq*psi_sigmasq)\n",
    "  n <- length(psi_theta)\n",
    "  c(theta-error, sqrt(mean(phi_m^2)/n), theta+error, sqrt(mean(phi_p^2)/n))\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "sensitivity_bounds_r <- function(est_list, eta_ysq, eta_asq, alpha = NULL) {\n",
    "  res <- lapply(est_list, sensitivity_bounds_single_r,\n",
    "                eta_ysq=eta_ysq, eta_asq=eta_asq, alpha=alpha)\n",
    "  if (is.null(alpha)) {\n",
    "    return(c(mean(sapply(res, `[`, 1)), mean(sapply(res, `[`, 2))))\n",
    "  }\n",
    "  lower <- sapply(res,`[`,1); sl <- sapply(res,`[`,2)\n",
    "  upper <- sapply(res,`[`,3); su <- sapply(res,`[`,4)\n",
    "  z <- qnorm(1 - alpha)\n",
    "  c(mean(lower) - z*sqrt(mean(sl^2)+var(lower)),\n",
    "    mean(upper) + z*sqrt(mean(su^2)+var(upper)))\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "tvalue_r <- function(est_list, value=0, leq=NULL, alpha=NULL) {\n",
    "  t_out <- 1\n",
    "  for (t in seq(0, 1, length.out=1000L)) {\n",
    "    b <- sensitivity_bounds_r(est_list, t, t, alpha=alpha)\n",
    "    if (is.null(leq) && value>=b[1] && value<=b[2]) { t_out <- t; break }\n",
    "    if (!is.null(leq) && leq  && value>=b[1])        { t_out <- t; break }\n",
    "    if (!is.null(leq) && !leq && value<=b[2])         { t_out <- t; break }\n",
    "  }\n",
    "  t_out\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "# -- PLM (DML residuals) sensitivity ------------------------------------------\n",
    "\n",
    "dml_sensitivity_bounds_single_r <- function(est, eta_ysq, eta_asq, alpha = NULL) {\n",
    "  nusq    <- mean(est$Dres^2)\n",
    "  theta   <- mean(est$yres * est$Dres) / nusq\n",
    "  sigmasq <- mean((est$yres - est$Dres * theta)^2)\n",
    "  S       <- sqrt(sigmasq / nusq)\n",
    "  Casq    <- eta_asq / (1 - eta_asq)\n",
    "  error   <- S * sqrt(Casq * eta_ysq)\n",
    "  if (is.null(alpha)) return(c(theta - error, theta + error))\n",
    "  n           <- length(est$yres)\n",
    "  psi_theta   <- (est$yres - est$Dres * theta) * est$Dres / nusq\n",
    "  psi_sigmasq <- (est$yres - est$Dres * theta)^2 - sigmasq\n",
    "  psi_nusq    <- est$Dres^2 - nusq\n",
    "  k <- sqrt(Casq * eta_ysq) / (2 * S)\n",
    "  phi_p <- psi_theta + k*(-(sigmasq/nusq^2)*psi_nusq + (1/nusq)*psi_sigmasq)\n",
    "  phi_m <- psi_theta - k*(-(sigmasq/nusq^2)*psi_nusq + (1/nusq)*psi_sigmasq)\n",
    "  c(theta-error, sqrt(mean(phi_m^2)/n), theta+error, sqrt(mean(phi_p^2)/n))\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "dml_sensitivity_bounds_r <- function(est_list, eta_ysq, eta_asq, alpha = NULL) {\n",
    "  res <- lapply(est_list, dml_sensitivity_bounds_single_r,\n",
    "                eta_ysq=eta_ysq, eta_asq=eta_asq, alpha=alpha)\n",
    "  if (is.null(alpha)) {\n",
    "    return(c(mean(sapply(res,`[`,1)), mean(sapply(res,`[`,2))))\n",
    "  }\n",
    "  lower <- sapply(res,`[`,1); sl <- sapply(res,`[`,2)\n",
    "  upper <- sapply(res,`[`,3); su <- sapply(res,`[`,4)\n",
    "  z <- qnorm(1 - alpha)\n",
    "  c(mean(lower) - z*sqrt(mean(sl^2)+var(lower)),\n",
    "    mean(upper) + z*sqrt(mean(su^2)+var(upper)))\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "dml_tvalue_r <- function(est_list, value=0, leq=NULL, alpha=NULL) {\n",
    "  t_out <- 1\n",
    "  for (t in seq(0, 1, length.out=1000L)) {\n",
    "    b <- dml_sensitivity_bounds_r(est_list, t, t, alpha=alpha)\n",
    "    if (is.null(leq) && value>=b[1] && value<=b[2]) { t_out <- t; break }\n",
    "    if (!is.null(leq) && leq  && value>=b[1])        { t_out <- t; break }\n",
    "    if (!is.null(leq) && !leq && value<=b[2])         { t_out <- t; break }\n",
    "  }\n",
    "  t_out\n",
    "}"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c016",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Short Estimates Under Conditional Ignorability"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 12,
   "id": "c017",
   "metadata": {
    "vscode": {
     "languageId": "r"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Main estimation loop matching the Python notebook structure.\n",
    "# estimator_fn(X, y, splits) returns list(estimates=c(point,se,lower,upper), model=...)\n",
    "generic_pipeline_r <- function(estimator_fn, q_grid, name, n_seeds = 5L) {\n",
    "  all_res  <- list()\n",
    "  all_ests <- list()\n",
    "  for (q in q_grid) {\n",
    "    cat(sprintf(\"q=%d\\n\", q))\n",
    "    est_mat   <- matrix(NA, n_seeds, 4L)\n",
    "    seed_ests <- list()\n",
    "    for (i in seq_len(n_seeds)) {\n",
    "      seed <- 122L + i\n",
    "      dat  <- get_data_r(q, region=region, synthetic=synthetic, random_seed=seed)\n",
    "      out  <- estimator_fn(dat$X, dat$y, dat$splits)\n",
    "      est_mat[i, ] <- out$estimates\n",
    "      seed_ests[[i]] <- out$model\n",
    "      cat(sprintf(\"  seed=%d: %.3f\\n\", seed, out$estimates[1]))\n",
    "    }\n",
    "    key <- sprintf(\"q=%d\", q)\n",
    "    all_res[[key]]  <- data.frame(\n",
    "      method = name,\n",
    "      point  = mean(est_mat[, 1]),\n",
    "      stderr = sqrt(mean(est_mat[, 2]^2) + var(est_mat[, 1]))\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    all_ests[[key]] <- seed_ests\n",
    "  }\n",
    "  list(res=all_res, ests=all_ests)\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "transform_res_to_df_r <- function(res_list, q_grid, alpha = NULL) {\n",
    "  rows <- list()\n",
    "  for (q in q_grid) {\n",
    "    key <- sprintf(\"q=%d\", q)\n",
    "    r   <- res_list[[key]]\n",
    "    if (!is.null(alpha)) {\n",
    "      z <- qnorm(1 - alpha)\n",
    "      lo <- r$point - z * r$stderr\n",
    "      hi <- r$point + z * r$stderr\n",
    "      rows[[key]] <- sprintf(\"%.2f (%.2f) [%.2f, %.2f]\", r$point, r$stderr, lo, hi)\n",
    "    } else {\n",
    "      rows[[key]] <- sprintf(\"%.2f\", r$point)\n",
    "    }\n",
    "  }\n",
    "  as.data.frame(rows, check.names=FALSE)\n",
    "}"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c018",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Nonparametric Model\n",
    "\n",
    "The first specification leaves the short regression $g_s(D, X^o)$ unrestricted. The Riesz representer is estimated from the Riesz loss using sieve candidates (degree-1 and degree-2 polynomial features crossed with covariates), selected by cross-validated Riesz score. Random forests are used for the regression model. Note: the Python notebook additionally considers a generalized random forest Riesz representer (ForestRiesz); that candidate is omitted here as it has no direct R equivalent."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 13,
   "id": "c019",
   "metadata": {
    "vscode": {
     "languageId": "r"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "nonlinrr_r <- function(X, y, splits) {\n",
    "  rr_factory <- rr_fn_gen(X, moment_fn, splits)\n",
    "  get_reg    <- reg_fn_gen(X, y, splits)\n",
    "\n",
    "  fit <- debiased_moment_fit(X, y, moment_fn, rr_factory, get_reg, splits)\n",
    "  list(estimates = avg_moment_r(fit, alpha = 0.1), model = fit)\n",
    "}"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 14,
   "id": "c020",
   "metadata": {
    "vscode": {
     "languageId": "r"
    }
   },
